{
  "what": "Pre-registered re-test of zero-shot TimesFM (BigQuery AI.FORECAST) as Anumaan's 14-day demand forecast. All data SYNTHETIC (anumaan.sim), scored against the simulator's GROUND TRUTH true_use.",
  "rules": {
    "written_at": "2026-09-30T20:22:21Z",
    "status": "Written before any query of this re-test ran. Results are added below it; this block is not edited afterwards.",
    "model": "'TimesFM 2.5' in BigQuery AI.FORECAST (GA; the default model in the AI.FORECAST reference updated 2026-09-29): zero-shot, univariate, no covariates. Project anumaan-c4c, dataset anumaan_forecast, asia-south1.",
    "setup": "anumaan.forecast.evaluate_forecast as it stands: sim.simulate(seed) with behaviour 'default' (36 PHCs x 7 conditions x 200 days); origins every 14 days from day 45 (11 per seed); each origin's series cut at day <= origin; 14-day horizon; forecast diagnoses x the grammar's units per diagnosis = 14-day demand per PHC x primary drug.",
    "score": "All-cells WAPE per seed: sum |forecast - true_use| / sum true_use over every origin x PHC x primary drug.",
    "candidates": {
      "grain": {
        "day": "AI.FORECAST on daily diagnosis counts, horizon 14 days.",
        "week": "AI.FORECAST on weekly totals counted back from each origin (week 0 ends on the origin; the oldest, partial week is dropped), horizon 2 weeks; each week's forecast is spread evenly over its 7 days."
      },
      "point": {
        "q50": "forecast_value (the median), from confidence_level 0.8.",
        "q55": "prediction_interval_upper_bound from confidence_level 0.1.",
        "q60": "prediction_interval_upper_bound from confidence_level 0.2.",
        "qmean": "0.3 x lower + 0.4 x forecast_value + 0.3 x upper, from confidence_level 0.8: the 30/40/30 quantile mean, assuming the 80% bounds are q10 and q90."
      },
      "ets_weight": [0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75],
      "blend": "forecast = w x ETS + (1 - w) x TimesFM, on the 14-day units after the same CRG step. ETS = the damped-trend ETS already in anumaan/forecast.py (the 'crg' arm; its grid was tuned on seeds 0-4 before this re-test).",
      "plus": "ETS alone (w = 1).",
      "count": "2 grains x 4 points x 4 weights + ETS alone = 33"
    },
    "selection_queries": "Seeds 0-4 only: 6 queries (day and week x confidence_level 0.8, 0.1, 0.2). q50 and qmean share the 0.8 query; the blends are computed offline.",
    "criterion": "Mean over seeds 0-4 of the all-cells WAPE, unrounded. Lowest wins.",
    "ties": "Every candidate within 0.001 of the lowest mean counts as tied, and the simplest tied candidate wins. Simplest first: ETS alone (the incumbent, no cloud call); then TimesFM candidates by their number of departures from day / q50 / w = 0 (weekly grain, a point other than q50, and w > 0 each count 1). Equal simplicity: lower mean WAPE.",
    "report": "The whole seeds 0-4 table. The winner once on seeds 5-9 and once on seeds 10-14, each against ETS alone on the same seeds (per seed, mean, range). Nothing is re-chosen after seeds 5-9 or 10-14 are seen.",
    "if_ets_alone_wins": "Say so plainly: TimesFM stays a benchmark.",
    "information_only": "When the query budget allows, the best TimesFM-alone candidate (w = 0) by the same criterion is also run once on seeds 5-9 and once on 10-14. It cannot change the decision.",
    "ui": "The forecast endpoint gets a TimesFM line only if the winner is a TimesFM candidate and its mean WAPE is below ETS alone on both seeds 5-9 and seeds 10-14.",
    "reference": "The plain history mean (the 'crg_mean' arm) is shown for context. It is not a candidate.",
    "failures": "A query that fails for a mechanical reason (SQL, quota, parsing) may be fixed and re-run within the budget. A candidate that still cannot be scored is reported as missing.",
    "queries": "At most 10 AI.FORECAST queries in all, each about 10 MB billed (inside the free tier); free dry runs are not counted. Tables dx_synthetic_0_4, dx_synthetic_5_9 and dx_synthetic_10_14 (new, one per seed set). dx_synthetic, which the default --bigquery run writes, is not touched. The raw AI.FORECAST rows are kept locally.",
    "disclosure": [
      "On 29 Sep 2026 TimesFM was already scored on seeds 5-9 at day grain: q50 with TimesFM 3.0 (WAPE 0.085-0.093, the README figure) and with TimesFM 2.5 (0.084-0.094), and the 30/40/30 quantile mean (qmean, 0.075-0.082), which was looked at on seeds 5-9 only. Seeds 5-9 are therefore not clean for day-grain q50 and qmean; seeds 10-14 are the clean test.",
      "Seeds 10-14 have never been used to score a forecast. The only earlier use found in the project's sessions is seed 11 in a start-up timing check of a different network shape (1 state x 14 x 5 PHCs, 120 days).",
      "The weekly grain and the q55/q60 points were suggested on 1 Oct 2026 by a local stand-in (a median of past counts, not TimesFM) run on seeds 0-4 only.",
      "The ETS grid was tuned on seeds 0-4, so on seeds 0-4 both sides are in-sample."
    ]
  },
